      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Heap</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Top-k</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Design</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/kth-largest-element-in-a-stream/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 703</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Kth Largest Element in a Stream</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Keep only the k largest values in a min-heap: its top is the weakest of the top k, which is exactly the kth largest. A new value either beats the top (swap it in) or can never matter again. O(log k) per add, O(k) memory, no matter how long the stream is.</p>\n"
  },
